<AashaCare /><section class="seo-hero"><p class="seo-kicker">Greater Noida clinic</p><h1>Psychiatrist in Greater Noida</h1>
<div class="seo-answer"><strong>Direct answer:</strong> Dr. Anita Sharma is a Consultant Psychiatrist at Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic, J123 Gamma II, Greater Noida. Adults can request a psychiatry consultation to discuss their concerns and possible next steps. Child and adolescent care is coordinated through Aasha Early Intervention Centre.</div><p class="seo-lead">Consult Dr. Anita Sharma in Gamma II. See what a first psychiatry visit involves, review current fees and directions, then request an appointment.</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="/book">Request a psychiatry appointment</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/fees">View psychiatry fees</a></div></section><section class="seo-section"><h2>Consult Dr. Anita Sharma in Gamma II</h2><p>Mind Grace is based in Greater Noida and provides adult psychiatry consultations in person, with online consultations available through the clinic's teleconsultation pathway. A psychiatric visit is a conversation about the situation that brought you in, relevant health and personal history, and the options that may be appropriate. You do not need to arrive with a confirmed diagnosis or a perfectly organised explanation.</p><p>Dr. Anita Sharma's role is described on her <a href="/dr-anita-sharma">psychiatrist profile</a>. Her profile and the <a href="/doctors">clinical team page</a> provide more information about who is involved in care. For child or adolescent care, start with <a href="/aasha">Aasha</a>, which has a separate booking route and service information.</p><h2>What happens in a first psychiatry consultation?</h2><p>The first conversation may cover the concern, when it began, what has changed over time, and its effect on sleep, work, study, relationships, physical health, and day-to-day routines. The clinician may ask about previous treatment, current medicines, health conditions, family context, and what has already helped. You can say when you do not know or do not feel ready to answer something.</p><h3>Your concerns and relevant history</h3><p>If you have previous prescriptions, discharge summaries, investigation results, or a short list of current medicines, these can help provide context. Bring only what is relevant and available; do not delay asking for care because a record is missing. You may bring a trusted person if that helps you feel comfortable, while the clinician may also make time to hear from you directly. More practical preparation is on the <a href="/process">first-visit guide</a>.</p><h3>Options, decisions and follow-up</h3><p>After understanding the situation, the clinician can explain possible next steps. Depending on the consultation, this may involve discussing medication, therapy, additional assessment, a referral, or a follow-up conversation. Medication is not automatic, and no particular treatment or result can be promised in advance. You can ask about expected benefits, possible side effects, alternatives, monitoring, and when to seek review before making an informed decision.</p><p>Psychiatry and therapy can sometimes be part of coordinated care, but the right combination depends on a person's needs and preferences. Learn about <a href="/therapy">clinical psychology and therapy</a> or compare roles in the <a href="/psychiatrist-vs-psychologist">psychiatrist and psychologist guide</a>.</p><h2>Fees, clinic hours and directions</h2><p>The fees page lists the current consultation rate and duration, as well as other services. Review <a href="/fees#psychiatry">psychiatry fees</a> before you request a visit, and use <a href="/location">directions to J123, Gamma II</a> to plan travel. Online appointments are explained on the <a href="/teleconsultation">teleconsultation page</a>; requesting an online appointment and attending by video are distinct steps, and the team can confirm available options.</p><p>For travel from Noida or elsewhere in the NCR, check the address and route in your preferred navigation app before leaving. The clinic does not publish unverified travel times or landmark-specific directions. If a route, accessibility detail, or parking question affects your visit, contact reception before setting out.</p><h2>Questions before you book</h2><h3>Can I request an online consultation?</h3><p>Yes, you can ask about an online consultation through the clinic's appointment channels. The team will confirm whether a video visit is suitable and available. See the <a href="/teleconsultation">online consultation information</a> for preparation and practical details.</p><h3>Where do I book an appointment for a child?</h3><p>All child-related care on this site is coordinated through <a href="/aasha">Aasha Early Intervention Centre</a>. Families can review the age-appropriate service pathway and submit a request using <a href="/aasha/book">Aasha's booking page</a>.</p><h3>What should I compare when choosing a psychiatrist?</h3><p>Look for a clearly stated medical and specialist role, information that helps you decide whether the clinician's scope fits your concern, a transparent fee and visit duration, a practical location or online option, and an explained follow-up process. Search labels such as “best” cannot tell you whether an appointment is the right fit. You can review Dr. Sharma's <a href="/dr-anita-sharma">profile</a>, the <a href="/fees">fees</a>, and the <a href="/process">visit steps</a> before deciding.</p><p>Mind Grace is not an emergency or crisis service. If there is immediate danger, call 112 or go to the nearest emergency department; see <a href="/emergency">urgent help information</a>.</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="/book">Request a psychiatry appointment</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/contact">Contact the clinic</a></div></section>
    <section class="seo-section"><h2>Hospital-specific search results</h2><p>This page describes Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic at J-123, Gamma II, Greater Noida. A search mentioning Yatharth Hospital, Sharda Hospital, or another hospital does not establish that a Mind Grace clinician practises there or is affiliated with it. If you want an appointment at a particular hospital, check that hospital’s current official doctor directory and contact its booking desk directly. For a Mind Grace consultation, use the clinic’s published address, fees and booking information on this site.</p></section>
